    {
      "$schema": "https://ui.shadcn.com/schema/registry-item.json",
      "name": "loopback-widget",
      "type": "registry:file",
      "title": "Loopback capture widget",
      "description": "The embeddable feedback widget itself: a dependency-free vanilla-JS IIFE that renders a floating toolbar, lets a user pin feedback on any element, auto-captures failing requests with their response bodies, console trail and AI run metadata, and turns pins green when an agent verifies the fix. Framework-agnostic \u2014 it runs in a shadow root and never touches your styles.",
      "author": "Dikshant Joshi <https://github.com/joshidikshant>",
      "categories": [
        "feedback",
        "devtools"
      ],
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "widget/loopback-widget.js",
          "type": "registry:file",
          "target": "~/public/loopback-widget.js"
        }
      ],
      "docs": "Load it with your project slug and a running Loopback hub (loopback-mcp-server --http):\n\n<script src=\"/loopback-widget.js\" data-project=\"my-app\" data-endpoint=\"http://127.0.0.1:7077\"></script>\n\nIn Next.js, render it from the root layout with next/script (strategy=\"afterInteractive\"). The widget owns its own theme and reads none of your CSS variables, so it looks the same on every site."
    }
